{"id": "holcim-2026-07-21-014", "date": "2026-07-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["holcim"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Cementos Pacasmayo announces financial results for the first half of 2026", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/peru-currency-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Peru:</strong> Cementos Pacasmayo, a subsidiary of Holcim,&nbsp;announced today its consolidated results for the first six months of 2026 and the second quarter. For the six months, cement sales volumes increased by 14% year-on-year, mainly due to increased demand for bagged cement. Revenues increased by 13%, in line with increased sales volumes. Consolidated earnings before interest, taxation, depreci", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21021-cementos-pacasmayo-announces-financial-results-for-the-first-half-of-2026", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-21-015", "date": "2026-07-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Cimaf to expand grinding capacity to 1.8Mt by September 2026", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/approved-licence-construction-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Gabon: </strong>Cimaf is preparing to commission its third US$43m cement grinding line, scheduled for September 2026. The project was presented to the President of Gabon on 20 May 2026 by a delegation led by Cimaf CEO Anas Sefrioui. It will more than double the company’s production capacity from 0.85Mt/yr to 1.85Mt/yr. It is also expected to reduce cement imports and provide 350 jobs fo", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21020-cimaf-to-expand-grinding-capacity-to-1-8mt-by-september-2026", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-21-016", "date": "2026-07-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Alternative fuels trial at Adbri prompts backlash", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/australia-south-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Australia: </strong>Adbri’s cement plant in Adelaide has received approval to burn more plastic waste as alternative fuel for its kiln, in a decision a local council is seeking to challenge in the courts, according to ABC news. The South Australia Environment Protection Authority (EPA) earlier in July 2026 approved a six-week trial permitting&nbsp;Adbri&nbsp;to use&nbsp;greater amounts of refuse-deri", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21018-alternative-fuels-trial-at-adbri-prompts-backlash", "type": "rss"}]}
